{"name":"PSL scale","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":23,"casual":{"lead":["PSL stands for Perceived Sexual Levels, an informal scale used in looksmaxxing communities to rate facial attractiveness, usually from 1 to 8. Its name is said to combine three forum sites on which it arose.","It sets out tiers from below average through 'normie' and 'Chadlite' up to 'Chad' and beyond. Sources describe it as subjective and not scientifically validated."],"sections":[{"h":"How it works","paras":["Raters judge faces on features that community explanations group under harmony, dimorphism, angularity and individual features. Because individual raters differ, scores vary; forum users also debate whether PSL differs from what they call 'appeal', a broader notion of attractiveness."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks and caveats","paras":["The scale itself carries no physical risk. Commentators cited by Wikipedia criticize the surrounding culture for tiering people and link it to body dysmorphia and distress; the Wikipedia article also carries a neutrality-dispute tag."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"A chemosensory system that regulates biofilm formation through modulation of cyclic diguanylate levels.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16186483/","source":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","year":2005,"cites":625,"kind":null},{"title":"PTEN: one gene, many syndromes.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12938083/","source":"Human mutation","year":2003,"cites":552,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Tabix: fast retrieval of sequence features from generic TAB-delimited files.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21208982/","source":"Bioinformatics (Oxford, England)","year":2011,"cites":529,"kind":null},{"title":"Pel is a cationic exopolysaccharide that cross-links extracellular DNA in the Pseudomonas aeruginosa biofilm matrix.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26311845/","source":"Proceedings of the National Aca